With `--additional-axioms`, an application of a function stored in a field of type `A -> T` of an inductive datatype value, or of type `A --> T` where its precondition holds, is strictly below that value in the termination order, as the elements of a `seq`, `set` or `map` field already are (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/326). For example, `Count(f(0))` in a function over `datatype Ord = Zero | Succ(Ord) | Lim(f: nat -> Ord)` now passes its termination check. Fields of type `A ~> T` and fields of codatatypes get no such fact. The option remains disabled by default.
